Root cause of the earlier timeout (step 25, fb_audit_design_optimization.py),
investigated rather than assumed: bounded_single_model_extrema runs an 801x801
grid whenever a model's audit-CI box straddles alpha+beta=1 (common for this
project's thin per-model audits), and the greedy search inside that script
re-evaluated all 136 pairs from scratch for ~34 candidate cells at ~24 budget
steps without noticing 16 of 17 models' boxes were unchanged between trials --
confirmed by profiling in isolation (still running past 300s with nothing else
competing). Fixed with a local functools.lru_cache wrapper (fb_audit_design_
optimization.py, commit cda1b93) -- a pure-function cache, not an approximation;
verified the fixed script's JSON output is byte-for-byte identical to the
pre-fix committed file, and that two consecutive runs are byte-identical to
each other (deterministic, no hidden RNG). Runtime for that one step in this
full run: 2.7s (previously >300s and still running when manually stopped).

